# The Dockerfile stands alone: it pip-installs from PyPI and needs no other
# file from the repository, so someone who downloads the sdist can build the
# image from it. setuptools ships only what it knows about, and it does not
# know about this, so v0.8.2 shipped without it.
include Dockerfile

# The documents a reader of the source would look for first.
include CHANGELOG.md
include SECURITY.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md

# Not the docs tree, the wiki, or the PDFs. They are large, they are not
# needed to build or run anything, and the repository is one link away.
